<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#SemioticProjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Semiotic Projection is about the projection of the User seeing the meme onto a certain part of the meme. The projection could be onto some VisualMaterial or some TextualMaterial or some Scene."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01526#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a smiling cashier in a retail setting, holding a payment terminal, with overlaid text that reads 'put the money in a bag. now! that will be $0.15'. The scene is a common retail checkout scenario. The text is absurd and nonsensical, suggesting a joke or satire about the triviality of a transaction or the absurdity of being charged for something like 'putting money in a bag'. There is no indication of toxicity, harmfulness, abuse, cyberbullying, misogyny, or propaganda. The intent is purely humorous and satirical, using the juxtaposition of a mundane retail interaction with an illogical, exaggerated instruction to create comedic effect. The visual elements (cashier, store, payment terminal) are neutral and do not carry any stereotypical or harmful markers. The meme relies on the incongruity between the visual context and the text to generate humor, not on targeting or degrading any group or individual."@en .
