<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#ColorComposition> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Color Composition elements from the image. Color Composition includes: color schemes, color palettes, color contrasts, dominant colors, color patterns, and color arrangements. For each color element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'dominant_red', 'color_contrast'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the dominant red color', 'the color contrast'), 3) A brief description of the color's role and visual impact. Focus on colors that are significant to the meme's visual composition and meaning. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"dominant_red\", \"label\": \"the dominant red color\", \"description\": \"Bright red flames that dominate the background, creating a sense of danger and urgency\"}"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#ComparativePositioning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text positioned between elements being compared or contrasted in memes"@en .
