<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Textual Material elements from the image. Textual Material includes: captions, text overlays, speech bubbles, written words, phrases, sentences, and any visible text. For each textual element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'main_caption', 'speech_bubble_text'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the main caption', 'the speech bubble text'), 3) A brief description of the text content and its context. Focus on all visible text elements that contribute to the meme's meaning. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"main_caption\", \"label\": \"the main caption\", \"description\": \"The text 'This is fine' written in bold letters at the bottom of the image\"}"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Complementarity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Complementarity"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#comparativelyPositionedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:nefbf8fc3ba76434fb3332223cc99e279b7 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#objectEmbeddedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "object embedded in"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#compositionallyIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates compositional design integration between dimension instances"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Dimension> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Visual Material includes: people, objects, characters, scenes, graphics, and any salient visual elements."@en .
